Accepted evidence:
- clean three-file, open/mergeable GitHub evidence PR;
- exact Darwin publication head remains 83f1dae7ccba09832cac996316323f2829fee7a3;
- publication checkout has only a local bare remote;
- no Forgejo credential helper is configured;
- tea/gh are absent;
- no existing Forgejo-capable opaque helper/client/session was found;
- no credential material was requested, read, or published;
- authenticated publication, PR creation and independent manifest verification remain absent.

Critical representation defect:
The CAPABILITY_REQUEST principal is written as “codex@wolfram.local acting through the authorized Darwin publication identity.” That is an organizational actor/role, not the exact Forgejo provider account principal. Credential enrollment must bind three distinct identities:
1. requesting organizational actor/role;
2. exact provider principal/account;
3. exact resource and verbs.

Do not ask Pasha to authorize or enroll an ambiguous principal. The stated post-enrollment “credential-free authenticated read” must instead mean a fresh process using an opaque handle/helper without rendering the secret.

First broken transition:
healthy Forgejo/tailnet route -> exact provider-principal-bound credential relationship -> repo-scoped Git/PR capability.

Minimum next safe continuation:
- resolve the exact existing Forgejo account/principal through non-secret account/repository metadata;
- define a deterministic Keychain/SecurityManager handle bound to provider principal + chitakasha/gd2 + read/push-branch/create-PR;
- prepare a one-time enrollment ceremony whose success can be tested by a fresh process without revealing the execution secret;
- only then present one human-presence request.

Settlement audit:
CLAIMED and EXECUTION_FINISHED exist; no TASK_COMPLETED/TASK_BLOCKED receipt appeared during review. Process exit and report publication are not terminal settlement.

No model identity, effort, token usage, or run-level quota attribution was exposed; none is claimed.
